# Force LF on shell scripts even when checked out on Windows. A CR at
# the end of the shebang line makes Linux refuse to exec the script
# ("/bin/sh^M: no such file or directory"), and the installers run on
# Linux runners and on end-user Linux/macOS machines.
*.sh text eol=lf

# Same reasoning for the bash pre-commit hook and PowerShell scripts
# (PowerShell is tolerant of CRLF but Windows Git Bash autocrlf can
# still cause diff noise). Normalise.
.githooks/* text eol=lf
*.ps1 text eol=crlf

# Go toolchain (gofmt, go vet, staticcheck) requires LF. The pre-commit
# hook runs gofmt -l against go/; without these rules core.autocrlf=true
# on Windows converts LF→CRLF on checkout and every Go file fails gofmt.
*.go    text eol=lf
go.mod  text eol=lf
go.sum  text eol=lf
